R4A: backport from busybox master (libbb/lineedit.c).

With LI_INTERRUPTIBLE (set by ash), 1.36.1 aborted line editing on ANY
EINTR — including the one caused by SIGWINCH when the terminal is resized
(e.g. the on-screen keyboard opening or closing). ash then wrote "\n" and
returned an empty line, so every resize printed a fresh prompt. Upstream
master only bails out when a real signal handler set bb_got_signal; the
SIGWINCH handler does not, so a resize just redraws the line in place.

--- a/libbb/lineedit.c	2026-11-21 17:57:43.552529800 -0300
+++ b/libbb/lineedit.c	2026-11-21 17:57:43.603244400 -0300
@@ -2197,14 +2197,16 @@
 			IF_FEATURE_EDITING_WINCH(S.ok_to_redraw = 0;)
 			if (errno != EINTR)
 				break;
+			/* It was EINTR. Repeat read_key() unless... */
 			if (state->flags & LI_INTERRUPTIBLE) {
-				/* LI_INTERRUPTIBLE bails out on EINTR,
-				 * but nothing really guarantees that bb_got_signal
-				 * is nonzero. Follow the least surprise principle:
+				/* LI_INTERRUPTIBLE bails out on EINTR
+				 * if bb_got_signal became nonzero.
+				 * (It may stay zero: for example, our SIGWINCH
+				 * handler does not set it. This is used for signals
+				 * which should not interrupt line editing).
 				 */
-				if (bb_got_signal == 0)
-					bb_got_signal = 255;
-				goto ret;
+				if (bb_got_signal != 0)
+					goto ret; /* will return -1 */
 			}
 		}
 
